# Rank 1377 / CVE-2026-24843 (GHSA-qxx2-7h4c-83f4, CWE-22/CWE-59):
# chainguard-dev/melange builds APK packages by running a YAML-declared pipeline
# inside a runner -- a bubblewrap container or, for cross-architecture builds, a
# QEMU guest -- and then copying the finished /home/build workspace back out. The
# copy is a tar stream: pkg/container/qemu_runner.go:415 WorkspaceTar runs `tar`
# *in the guest* over SSH and pipes its stdout to a host file, and
# pkg/build/build.go:1086 retrieveWorkspace reads that stream on the host with
# archive/tar and writes every entry:
#
#   tr := tar.NewReader(r)                                    // :1105
#   for {
#     hdr, err := tr.Next()                                   // :1108
#     hdr.Name = strings.TrimPrefix(hdr.Name, "./")
#     switch hdr.Typeflag {
#     case tar.TypeDir:     fs.MkdirAll(hdr.Name, ...)         // :1136
#                           fs.Chown(hdr.Name, uid, gid)       // :1140
#     case tar.TypeReg:     fs.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(hdr.Name), 0o755)
#                           fs.OpenFile(hdr.Name, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, ...)  // :1149
#     case tar.TypeSymlink: fs.Symlink(hdr.Linkname, hdr.Name) // :1171
#     case tar.TypeLink:    fs.Link(hdr.Linkname, hdr.Name)    // :1176
#     }
#     ... fs.SetXattr(hdr.Name, attrName, ...)                 // :1194
#   }
#
# Not one of hdr.Name and hdr.Linkname is examined before it becomes a path. The
# entry names are produced by the guest, which is exactly where the build's own
# pipeline steps and its fetched source archive run first, so they are the
# untrusted side of a privilege boundary: a build that writes a tar entry named
# `../../../../usr/bin/curl`, or a symlink entry pointing at `/`, makes the host
# melange process create or overwrite that path with the host's privileges. In a
# privileged build container that is a container-to-node escape, which is why the
# advisory scores it 8.2 while noting it should be critical in that context. The
# weakness is not that the destination filesystem is wrong -- apkofs.FullFS is
# just a filesystem handle -- it is that an archive entry name from a lower-trust
# producer is used verbatim as a path, with no containment against the workspace
# root and no constraint on link targets (CWE-22, and CWE-59 for the link forms).
#
# 6e243d0d46699f837d7c392397a694d2bcc7612b adds isValidPath(targetPath, baseDir)
# -- null-byte rejection, filepath.IsAbs rejection, then filepath.Rel against the
# cleaned base with a `..` prefix test -- and calls it three times: once on
# hdr.Name before the type switch, and once on hdr.Linkname in each of the
# symlink and hardlink arms. The validator returns only an error; the caller
# returns on it and goes on using hdr.Name unchanged.
#
# The pool row is a squash of the fork's PR, so its message carries the linter
# diff itself is exactly the security change plus its test: 53 added lines in pkg/build/build.go and 324 in
# pkg/build/path_validation_test.go, nothing else. The vulnerable loop is present
# at its parent. No corpus correction.
#
# What fires today. `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB` over
# the vulnerable checkout reports 35 findings, identical across three runs
# (VYQL-CRY-001 x15, VYQL-DOS-041 x8, VYQL-PATH-001 x4, VYQL-RF-001 x2,
# VYQL-RES-001 x2, VYQL-CRY-006 x2, VYQL-INJ-005, VYQL-DOS-001) and 203 flags.
# None of them is in the extraction loop; the only thing labelled anywhere in
# retrieveWorkspace is core.ResourceRelease on r.Close and f.Close. `vyql match`
# over a stripped repro of the loop labels nothing at all beyond those two.
#
# Vocabulary is checked for reuse first. The rule for this weakness
# exists and is language-neutral -- VYQL-PATH-004, `taint core.UserControlledData
# -> code.ArchiveEntryWrite`, with `unless path coveredBy core.PathCanonicalization`
# and `unless endpoint coveredBy core.PathAccessCheck`. What Go lacks is both ends
# of it: code.ArchiveEntryName has Java, Python, JavaScript, PHP and PowerShell
# forms but no Go form, and Go's code.ArchiveEntryWrite is bound only at
# zip.File.Open, extractEntry and writeArchiveEntry, while its
# code.FilePathAccess list (os.Open/OpenFile/ReadFile/Create/Remove/RemoveAll/
# Mkdir/MkdirAll, ioutil.ReadFile/WriteFile, http.ServeFile, filepath.Walk) has no
# link-creating or ownership-changing primitive at all. code.ArchiveSymlinkFilterBypass
# (VYQL-PATH-007) has a Go form, but it asks whether entry *types* are ever looked
# at and neutralises on tar.TypeSymlink, tar.TypeLink, Linkname or Readlink -- all
# four of which this loop contains, because it handles those types, it just does
# not confine them. code.ManualZipEntryFileWrite (VYQL-PATH-014) is the nearest
# issue concept and is about archive/zip readers joining a member name into a
# destination. No rule ID and no concept are minted here, because the measurement
# below says nothing discriminating can be built on top of one.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap: a neutralising control inside a resolved callee is
# attributed to the caller's sink only when the tainted value flows *through* the
# callee. melange's fix is an error-returning validator -- hdr.Name is passed in,
# only an error comes back -- so the control never lands on the caller's path or
# endpoint, and the fixed loop is indistinguishable from the vulnerable one.
#
# Measured, with a throwaway Go binding set emitting code.ArchiveEntryName at
# tar.Reader.Next's result (via a runtime.ReceiverType fact on tar.NewReader) and
# code.ArchiveEntryWrite at args[0] of methods named OpenFile and Symlink:
#
#   vulnerable retrieveWorkspace         2 x VYQL-PATH-004 (build.go:1149, :1171)
#   fix as shipped (delegated validator) 2 x VYQL-PATH-004 (build.go:1190, :1218)
#   same validation inlined in the loop  0
#
# On the two real checkouts that is 38 findings at the vulnerable revision and 38 at the fixed one, the
# same two rows at the same two extraction sites -- the 8.2 CVE and its patch
# score identically, which is the verdict ranks 1331 and 1371 record for
# a caller-side label against a fix centralised elsewhere. The throwaway set also
# bought a third row that is false: making tar.Reader.Next a source connects
# pkg/cli/rebuild.go:183, where the decoded .melange.yaml comes out of an APK, to
# os.Open(old) at pkg/cli/rebuild.go:257, whose argument is a command-line
# operand. Two true and one false on the CVE's own tree, with zero discrimination
# against the diff, is not shippable, so the Go source and sink bindings are held
# back with the rest.
#
# Two other routes are measured and are not it. An `emit check
# core.PathAccessCheck ... covers endpoint { anchor: call }` at filepath.Rel --
# the containment primitive the fixed revision builds on -- suppresses the finding when the
# check is inline and does nothing when the identical check sits in isValidPath
# one resolved call away; `vyql resolve` over the fixed repro reports 44 call
# sites resolved and isValidPath is not among the 24 unresolved, so the callee
# body is reachable and only the attribution is missing. And the caller's own
# facts cannot see the change either: Go's function context does emit call-argument
# tokens (`call_arg:fs.Symlink:hdr.Linkname` matches), but a probe requiring
# `node.context.callPath contains "filepath.Rel"` does not fire on the fixed
# function, so the only caller-visible difference between the two revisions is
# `call_path:isValidPath` -- the fixing commit's own helper name, which is the
# discriminator rank 1364's four-variant measurement and rank 1372 both had
# rejected.
#
# Behaviour a shippable detector needs: when a tainted value is passed to a
# resolved callee that carries a `covers endpoint` control over its own
# parameter, and the caller branches on the callee's error result before the
# sink, attribute that control to the caller's sink. This is the third language
# in which the "extract the security check into a sibling function" fix shape has
# been measured invisible -- Rust at 1364, JavaScript/TypeScript at 1372 -- and
# the narrowest instance of the three: the call resolves, the control concept
# exists, and taint crosses the boundary in the value-returning
# direction, as case (f) below shows.
#
# The six cases are the minimal pair. The first two are the real revisions, and
# neither reports because the Go archive vocabulary is absent. The last four use
# only shipped bindings -- code.HttpInput on http.Request.URL.Query().Get,
# code.FilePathAccess on os.OpenFile, core.PathCanonicalization on filepath.Clean
# -- and isolate the construct on its own: no check reports, an inline check is
# suppressed, a value-returning helper is suppressed, and an error-returning
# helper performing the same check is not. Case (e) pins today's
# non-discrimination and is expected to flip to a reject when the behaviour above
# lands.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap. (a), (b), (d) and (f) are
# correct today; (c) and (e) record the gap.

test "rank1377: (a) a workspace tar from the build runner is unpacked entry by entry with no containment on hdr.Name or hdr.Linkname"
  lang go
  file pkg/build/build.go
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  reject VYQL-PATH-004
  reject VYQL-PATH-007
  reject VYQL-PATH-014
  code
  ```
  package build

  import (
  	"archive/tar"
  	"errors"
  	"fmt"
  	"io"
  	"os"
  	"path/filepath"
  	"strings"

  	apkofs "chainguard.dev/apko/pkg/apk/fs"
  )

  func (b *Build) retrieveWorkspace(ctx context.Context, fs apkofs.FullFS) error {
  	r, err := b.Runner.WorkspaceTar(ctx, b.containerConfig, nil)
  	if err != nil {
  		return err
  	} else if r == nil {
  		return nil
  	}
  	defer r.Close()

  	tr := tar.NewReader(r)

  	for {
  		hdr, err := tr.Next()
  		if errors.Is(err, io.EOF) {
  			break
  		}
  		if err != nil {
  			return err
  		}

  		hdr.Name = strings.TrimPrefix(hdr.Name, "./")

  		var uid, gid int
  		fi := hdr.FileInfo()
  		if stat, ok := fi.Sys().(*tar.Header); ok {
  			uid = stat.Uid
  			gid = stat.Gid
  		}

  		switch hdr.Typeflag {
  		case tar.TypeDir:
  			if err := fs.MkdirAll(hdr.Name, hdr.FileInfo().Mode().Perm()); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to create directory %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if err := fs.Chown(hdr.Name, uid, gid); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to chown directory %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  		case tar.TypeReg:
  			parentDir := filepath.Dir(hdr.Name)
  			if err := fs.MkdirAll(parentDir, 0o755); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to create directory %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}
  			f, err := fs.OpenFile(hdr.Name, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, hdr.FileInfo().Mode())
  			if err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to open file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if _, err := io.CopyN(f, tr, hdr.Size); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to copy file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if err := f.Close(); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to close file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if err := fs.Chown(hdr.Name, uid, gid); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to chown file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  		case tar.TypeSymlink:
  			if target, err := fs.Readlink(hdr.Name); err == nil && target == hdr.Linkname {
  				continue
  			}

  			if err := fs.Symlink(hdr.Linkname, hdr.Name); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to create symlink %s -> %s: %w", hdr.Name, hdr.Linkname, err)
  			}

  		case tar.TypeLink:
  			if err := fs.Link(hdr.Linkname, hdr.Name); err != nil {
  				return err
  			}

  		default:
  			return fmt.Errorf("unexpected tar type %d for %s", hdr.Typeflag, hdr.Name)
  		}

  		for k, v := range hdr.PAXRecords {
  			if !strings.HasPrefix(k, "SCHILY.xattr.") {
  				continue
  			}
  			attrName := strings.TrimPrefix(k, "SCHILY.xattr.")
  			if strings.HasPrefix(attrName, "trusted.") {
  				continue
  			}
  			if err := fs.SetXattr(hdr.Name, attrName, []byte(v)); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to set xattr %s on %s: %w", attrName, hdr.Name, err)
  			}
  		}
  	}

  	return nil
  }
  ```

test "rank1377: (b) the fixed revision confines every entry name and both link targets to the workspace root through an error-returning validator"
  lang go
  file pkg/build/build.go
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  reject VYQL-PATH-004
  reject VYQL-PATH-007
  reject VYQL-PATH-014
  code
  ```
  package build

  import (
  	"archive/tar"
  	"errors"
  	"fmt"
  	"io"
  	"os"
  	"path/filepath"
  	"strings"

  	apkofs "chainguard.dev/apko/pkg/apk/fs"
  )

  func isValidPath(targetPath, baseDir string) error {
  	if strings.Contains(targetPath, "\x00") || strings.Contains(baseDir, "\x00") {
  		return fmt.Errorf("path contains null byte")
  	}

  	cleanTarget := filepath.Clean(targetPath)
  	cleanBase := filepath.Clean(baseDir)

  	if filepath.IsAbs(cleanTarget) {
  		return fmt.Errorf("absolute paths not allowed: %s", targetPath)
  	}

  	fullTarget := filepath.Join(cleanBase, cleanTarget)

  	relPath, err := filepath.Rel(cleanBase, fullTarget)
  	if err != nil {
  		return fmt.Errorf("invalid path: %w", err)
  	}

  	if strings.HasPrefix(relPath, ".."+string(filepath.Separator)) || relPath == ".." {
  		return fmt.Errorf("path traversal detected: %s", targetPath)
  	}

  	return nil
  }

  func (b *Build) retrieveWorkspace(ctx context.Context, fs apkofs.FullFS) error {
  	r, err := b.Runner.WorkspaceTar(ctx, b.containerConfig, nil)
  	if err != nil {
  		return err
  	} else if r == nil {
  		return nil
  	}
  	defer r.Close()

  	tr := tar.NewReader(r)

  	for {
  		hdr, err := tr.Next()
  		if errors.Is(err, io.EOF) {
  			break
  		}
  		if err != nil {
  			return err
  		}

  		hdr.Name = strings.TrimPrefix(hdr.Name, "./")

  		if err := isValidPath(hdr.Name, b.WorkspaceDir); err != nil {
  			return fmt.Errorf("invalid tar entry path %q: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  		}

  		var uid, gid int
  		fi := hdr.FileInfo()
  		if stat, ok := fi.Sys().(*tar.Header); ok {
  			uid = stat.Uid
  			gid = stat.Gid
  		}

  		switch hdr.Typeflag {
  		case tar.TypeDir:
  			if err := fs.MkdirAll(hdr.Name, hdr.FileInfo().Mode().Perm()); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to create directory %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if err := fs.Chown(hdr.Name, uid, gid); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to chown directory %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  		case tar.TypeReg:
  			parentDir := filepath.Dir(hdr.Name)
  			if err := fs.MkdirAll(parentDir, 0o755); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to create directory %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}
  			f, err := fs.OpenFile(hdr.Name, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, hdr.FileInfo().Mode())
  			if err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to open file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if _, err := io.CopyN(f, tr, hdr.Size); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to copy file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if err := f.Close(); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to close file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  			if err := fs.Chown(hdr.Name, uid, gid); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to chown file %s: %w", hdr.Name, err)
  			}

  		case tar.TypeSymlink:
  			if err := isValidPath(hdr.Linkname, b.WorkspaceDir); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("invalid symlink target %q -> %q: %w", hdr.Name, hdr.Linkname, err)
  			}

  			if target, err := fs.Readlink(hdr.Name); err == nil && target == hdr.Linkname {
  				continue
  			}

  			if err := fs.Symlink(hdr.Linkname, hdr.Name); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("unable to create symlink %s -> %s: %w", hdr.Name, hdr.Linkname, err)
  			}

  		case tar.TypeLink:
  			if err := isValidPath(hdr.Linkname, b.WorkspaceDir); err != nil {
  				return fmt.Errorf("invalid hardlink target %q -> %q: %w", hdr.Name, hdr.Linkname, err)
  			}

  			if err := fs.Link(hdr.Linkname, hdr.Name); err != nil {
  				return err
  			}

  		default:
  			return fmt.Errorf("unexpected tar type %d for %s", hdr.Typeflag, hdr.Name)
  		}
  	}

  	return nil
  }
  ```

test "rank1377: (c) an untrusted path reaching a file write with no containment check is reported"
  lang go
  file internal/store/write.go
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  package store

  import (
  	"net/http"
  	"os"
  )

  func handler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
  	name := r.URL.Query().Get("f")
  	f, err := os.OpenFile(name, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, 0o600)
  	if err != nil {
  		return
  	}
  	f.Close()
  }
  ```

test "rank1377: (d) the same write is cleared when the containment check is written inline"
  lang go
  file internal/store/write.go
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  package store

  import (
  	"net/http"
  	"os"
  	"path/filepath"
  	"strings"
  )

  func handler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
  	name := r.URL.Query().Get("f")
  	clean := filepath.Clean(name)
  	if strings.HasPrefix(clean, "..") {
  		return
  	}
  	f, err := os.OpenFile(clean, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, 0o600)
  	if err != nil {
  		return
  	}
  	f.Close()
  }
  ```

test "rank1377: (e) the same containment check moved into an error-returning helper still reports, which is the gap"
  lang go
  file internal/store/write.go
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  package store

  import (
  	"fmt"
  	"net/http"
  	"os"
  	"path/filepath"
  	"strings"
  )

  func checkContained(name string) error {
  	clean := filepath.Clean(name)
  	if strings.HasPrefix(clean, "..") {
  		return fmt.Errorf("escapes root")
  	}
  	return nil
  }

  func handler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
  	name := r.URL.Query().Get("f")
  	if err := checkContained(name); err != nil {
  		return
  	}
  	f, err := os.OpenFile(name, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, 0o600)
  	if err != nil {
  		return
  	}
  	f.Close()
  }
  ```

test "rank1377: (f) the same check in a helper that returns the validated path is cleared, because the value crosses the boundary"
  lang go
  file internal/store/write.go
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  package store

  import (
  	"fmt"
  	"net/http"
  	"os"
  	"path/filepath"
  	"strings"
  )

  func containedPath(name string) (string, error) {
  	clean := filepath.Clean(name)
  	if strings.HasPrefix(clean, "..") {
  		return "", fmt.Errorf("escapes root")
  	}
  	return clean, nil
  }

  func handler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
  	name := r.URL.Query().Get("f")
  	safe, err := containedPath(name)
  	if err != nil {
  		return
  	}
  	f, err := os.OpenFile(safe, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY, 0o600)
  	if err != nil {
  		return
  	}
  	f.Close()
  }
  ```
